From 8f0ba0fe3b71fdd04c0c55030efa66249bea6945 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:30:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Track a function's named properties by shape
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Statics on a constructor function were a 100% cache miss — 0 hits out of
200 000, sloppy, strict and class alike — and that is how DeltaBlue reads
`Strength.REQUIRED` and `Strength.stronger` in its hot path.

Two prerequisites had to be fixed before the eligibility gate could be
flipped; without them flipping it would have been a correctness bug
rather than a no-op:

1. A function installed its own `length`, `name` and `prototype` with
   bare `ownProperties.Put`, and four constructors additionally took a
   shape-abandoning mutable ref through GetOwnProperties(). All are
   routed through FastAddValue now.
2. Every ordinary non-strict function carries the Annex B
   `caller`/`arguments` as deferred cells from birth, and a deferred cell
   abandoned the shape. Recorded with a NULL SLOT instead: the shape's
   *presence* claim needs no value, and its *absence* claim — "this
   object does not own K" — is what has to stay correct. A private name
   still abandons, being per-class-evaluation.

All four function rows go 0 → 199 999 and no site in the corpus abandons
a shape any more.

Also gates `prototype` out of the shape WRITE paths, which is a bug this
change would otherwise have introduced — and did, in an earlier draft.
JSFunction keeps its prototype in a cached field, and that field, not the
property, is what [[Construct]] reads; it is synced by overriding the
indexer, SetValue and DefineProperty. A shape fast path is none of those:
it writes ownProperties and shapeSlots and returns. So a cached store to
`f.prototype` updated the observable property and left `new` building
instances on the previous object.

That is DeltaBlue. Its `inheritsFrom` helper does
`this.prototype = new Inheriter()` from one emitted site, once per class,
so the first call missed and was correct and every call after it hit and
was not — leaving the second level of every inheritance chain unlinked
and `this.addConstraint` undefined two constructors down. The suite threw
before producing a score.

Fixed with a virtual JSObject.AllowsDirectShapeWrite(key), checked by
TryWriteShapeSlot, TryCreateShapeSlot and TryGetWritableShapeSlot.
Checked on the write and not only on the install: shapes are interned by
key set, so a JSFunction and a plain object carrying the same keys share
one shape AND one id, and an entry installed against the plain object
would otherwise hit the function. Reads are not gated — a read has no
field to keep in sync, so `f.prototype` still caches.

It is deliberately not the null-slot mechanism above. That works because
a deferred cell's stored value is not a JSValue, which the write paths
already reject; `prototype` holds an ordinary JSValue and sails through
every existing check. The comment claiming all three fast paths reject a
null slot was only ever true of the read path, and is corrected.

The fix costs nothing measurable: all 22 --cache-metrics rows are
byte-identical before and after, including all four function rows at
199 999, and a 2 M-iteration three-field constructor loop measures a
median paired ratio of 1.0015 against a build with the three call sites
removed. A DeltaBlue-shaped loop stays ~10% faster (median paired ratio
0.905 over five interleaved pairs).

20 test cases in PropertyShapeCacheTests: 13 on the Annex B surface —
`caller`/`arguments` keeping their non-writable, non-enumerable,
non-configurable DATA descriptor, reading `caller` while the function is
on the stack, the Function.prototype poison pills still throwing, a
null-slot key still reading through the generic path once warm, plus
`length`/`name`/`prototype` values, attributes and enumeration order,
redefinition, a bound function's name and length, a static redefined as
an accessor mid-loop, and delete revealing an inherited static. Seven
more on the write gate, including DeltaBlue's exact three-level
`inheritsFrom` idiom, one warmed site writing 300 functions' prototypes,
a class's non-writable prototype still refused once warm,
constructability surviving a non-object assignment, a function's other
statics still taking the store cache, and `prototype` still cached on
read.

Suite: 7 392 tests across 13 projects, 0 failures. Octane: 17 of 18
benchmarks pass, the one failure (RegExp's checksum) failing identically
on a pristine build at the pinned pointer.

Refs docs/performance-roadmap.md item 2-8.
